You see, in my language, "griz" means "to bite," and because grizozirg can bite on both sides with much power and little consideration for victim's welfare, its name has a reverse "griz" on the other end - "zirg". And "o" in middle connects them. Get it? Griz-o-zirg. It look like in mirror, errrrr... 

How you call it here...? 

Ah, a "polydrome," yes.&lt;end&gt;

